WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:03.730
We’ve covered a lot here on this channel,
and what you might have noticed about the

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:09.139
nature of our discoveries is that knowledge
is best broken down before digested.

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.989
Which is to say, if you are to learn how to
assemble a computer, it may benefit you also

00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:16.010
to see one taken apart.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.619
When you do so, you’ll notice in front of
you not a computer at all, but a collection

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.310
of individual parts.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.310
It’s in understanding these distinctive
parts in isolation that helps us shape our

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:32.259
awareness of their marriage, and how they
cooperate with one another to become their

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:33.600
collective self.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.899
Sure, this may be good practice, but then
tell me: how do we comprehend a whole that

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:43.710
is composed of parts unwilling to isolate
themselves from the rest?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:49.690
Because let’s face it, not all things, let
alone SCPs, can be torn apart for the convenience

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.840
of our study.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:56.540
No matter the subject we seek to understand,
it may choose to resist our deconstruction,

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.579
by one way or another.

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:04.190
Landmarks like the Temples of Malta and the
Pyramid of Djoser are held together by our

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.190
respect.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.690
Monuments like the Statue of Liberty are held
together by copper.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.760
The Family was held together by Charles Manson.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.450
But it’s not always the preservation of
history or elements of the periodic table

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.590
or psychopaths that reject humans' wishes
to disassemble.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:28.110
Far stronger than forces of nuts and bolts
are that of character and loyalty, and SCP-2085

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.540
is welded together by exactly that.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:37.070
SCP-2085 is a militant anarchist organization
consisting of six cybernetically-enhanced

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.950
individuals (A-1 through A-5 and B)

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.710
operating under the name Kuroi Usagi Shidan,
or more commonly known as the “Black Rabbit

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:47.710
Company.”

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:55.920
SCP-2085-A subjects are five adult female
augmented humans, designated SCP-2085-A-1

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.170
through SCP-2085-A-5.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:05.190
Subjects are genetic chimeras, each with an
estimated 6-10 different gene donors.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:11.709
They are fluent in Japanese, Mandarin Chinese,
Cantonese, Korean, Russian, and English, with

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:14.689
additional languages varying by individual.

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:19.489
Subjects display an array of genetic and cybernetic
enhancements, including genetic splices of

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:26.400
Felis catus physiology, having cat-like ears,
tails, and hair.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.209
These tails are prehensile and capable of
holding small objects, so if you’re accusing

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:34.950
one of them of stealing your pen, don’t
just go searching their pockets.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:40.040
They also have grip pads on hands and feet,
in case they ever did decide to retire from

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.620
anarchy and take up surfing.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.879
Their impressive features don’t stop there.

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:50.220
If they haven’t already put James Bond’s
gadgets to shame yet, just wait, Daniel Craig

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.360
is about to look like Dora the Explorer.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:03:00.720
SCP-2085-A-1 through A-5 all have ocular implants
with thermal vision, heads-up display, and

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.770
recording functionality.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:08.280
Also noted are carbon-nanoweave muscle fiber
augmentation, reinforced endoskeleton, and

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.129
brain-computer interface with internal hard
drive.

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:14.959
The list goes on, each etcetera more elaborate
than the next.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.870
Yet, what stands out most about them is not
a weapon but an attitude.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.980
These six members, although now held in isolation
from one another, do not show any signs of

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:30.599
splitting up, not even when under the heavy
pressure of The Foundation’s interrogation.

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:35.200
Agents spend their hours looking for cracks
to dig their fingers into, trying to get one

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.639
to betray the other and reveal sensitive information.

00:03:38.639 --> 00:03:44.060
But when asked to spill the beans, SCP-2085
screws the lid on tighter.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.590
They remain as a whole, resistant to our deconstruction.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:51.569
The agents get nowhere with their investigation.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.659
And with each minute wasted, it’s another
victory for SCP-2085.

00:03:56.659 --> 00:04:02.049
The hours go on and they keep stacking up
W’s, building momentum day after day, growing

00:04:02.049 --> 00:04:05.299
stronger and stronger as a unit.

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:10.629
As The Foundation tries to tear the group
apart, they respond with even greater resistance.

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:13.959
And this style of resistance is unique to
each member.

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:16.450
Imagine you are confronting SCP 2085-A-2.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:21.520
She is talkative, and so you think you might
get somewhere.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.241
You are all ears.

00:04:23.241 --> 00:04:29.100
But what SCP 2085-A-2 sees isn’t ears, but
troths.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.940
And she is happy to feed you her slop.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:38.310
She talks and talks and you listen closer
and closer, but all you are getting is misinformation.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.290
False names, inaccurate stories, dates that
don’t add up.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:48.680
You focus and follow along, only to find yourself
having run a marathon all the way to a dead

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.680
end.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:56.120
Now you are faced with SCP 2085-A-5, who takes
a different, more nonsensical approach.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:01.140
You are happy to no longer have to sift through
inaccuracies to decipher truths, but now,

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.120
there are no truths at all.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.910
All that you are given are absurdities.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.450
She speaks in ways that make you scratch your
head.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:14.100
Once saying, for no apparent reason, “I
take a hammer and I break my legs, I break

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.220
‘em for the better.”

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:19.140
After so many scratches you swear you’ve
dug an inch into your skin.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:25.310
And so you move on to SCP 2085-A-4 hoping
for better luck.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.100
She is straightforward with you.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.410
That much you like.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.940
But she’s hostile and doesn’t cooperate.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:33.840
When you ask her name, she raises her middle
finger.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.340
She tucks it back in to create a first.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.360
And then that fist punches the divider between
you.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.180
No amount of reinforced glass could make you
feel safe at that moment.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.350
Cracks spread.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:49.000
It looks like a web spun by a spider, and
you feel as small as one.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.280
Thankfully, a protective shutter is lowered.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.510
Aerosol sedatives are pumped into the containment
unit.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:06:00.070
She continues to try to escape, yelling profanities
even harsh for someone locked behind bars.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:05.720
Your ears have taken a beating from curse
words, nonsensical rambles, and heaps of misinformation.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.680
You want to lower your head into a toilet
bowl and hear nothing but water.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.070
Yes, that is where these women have driven
you.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.740
Your head to the bottom of a toilet bowl.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.700
You have put in so many hours, and yet you
have learned nothing new.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:25.110
And if you can’t learn anything new, you
might have to rely more on what you already

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.110
know.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.110
But what do you know?

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:31.650
Well, you know this: their track record is
quite impressive.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:37.680
Verified operations include smuggling, theft,
assault, vandalism, kidnapping, extortion,

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:43.710
property damage, possession of fissile materials,
corporate sabotage, embezzlement, identity

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:49.270
theft, fraud, copyright infringement, piracy,
possession transport and sale of anomalous

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.730
items, and tax evasion.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:57.920
Yet, when grilled under the heat of investigation,
they do not reveal any details about the nature

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.410
of these operations.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.960
You just know that they happened.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:07.820
All that is told is that SCP-2085 navigates
in such a way as to minimize the chance of

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:13.840
civilian casualties and maximize material
and morale damage to their target.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.020
They are proud of this.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:20.300
It seems as if SCP-2085 perceives themselves
on the side of good.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:25.910
While their list of operations on paper looks
like crimes, they stand proudly behind them,

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.070
pleading guilty with a grin.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.410
But behind every smile is more teeth.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.410
Teeth that go beyond saying cheese.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.820
Teeth hiding in the dark caves of a sealed
mouth.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:42.150
And you are determined to play dentist and
find your way in.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:46.250
But SCP-2085 doesn’t say awe for just anyone.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:51.470
So, how are you to understand a group that
resists our preferred methods of learning?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:56.250
How are you to properly assess the pieces
of a puzzle when the puzzle is glued tightly

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.270
together?

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.700
It starts at the top.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:04.800
Before you can decipher the motives of a nation,
you’d be smart to study their leader.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.260
And if you want to extrapolate the schemes
of a football team, you’d interview the

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.260
coach.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:15.070
And to truly know the moral of a television
show, you’d be better off asking the creator

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.680
than the actors.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:23.200
All of this is just to say, if you are to
ever understand the complexities of SCP-2085,

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:30.460
it is necessary you begin with SCP-2085-B,
the person pulling the string of the entire

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.519
operation for all of these years.

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:37.010
Now, you might be imagining a man of many
muscles.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.899
Someone able to fight a bear with an arm tied
behind his back.

00:08:40.899 --> 00:08:46.089
Someone who kicks through saloon doors, tilts
back his liquor, and walks out with a woman

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:47.340
in each arm.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:50.860
But you’d be dead wrong.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:56.829
SCP-2085-B, also known as Wizard, does not
look like an imposing lead at first glance,

00:08:56.829 --> 00:08:59.300
or even, at the hundredth glance.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.950
He is generally in very poor health and his
face shows it.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:10.500
He suffers from a variety of illnesses, most
notably a vitamin D deficiency, acute radiation

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:15.430
syndrome, and has unmanageable scarring from
severe and repeated skin ulceration.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:21.180
He doesn’t wear a cape and glamorous spandex
often found hanging in superheroes’ closets,

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:26.999
but instead he wears an Advanced Crew Escape
Suit accompanied by a cheap bathrobe and flimsy

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:29.019
red felt wizard's hat.

00:09:29.019 --> 00:09:32.529
He looks, with no elegant way of putting it,
like a dork.

00:09:32.529 --> 00:09:33.830
A goofball.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.120
A doofus.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.370
A…well, you get the point.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.639
Furthermore, he is an adult male human with
certain cybernetic and genetic enhancements.

00:09:41.639 --> 00:09:47.290
He has an adaptation of the gastrointestinal
tract to allow for an all-liquid diet.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:52.360
Within his suit, an esophageal input port
and waste output port are integrated.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:57.050
It is equipped with modifications to regulate
sweat, reduce abrasion damage from extended

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.920
usage, and aid in skin regeneration.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:05.509
His genetic enhancements include the replacement
of 11 previously missing digits on hands and

00:10:05.509 --> 00:10:11.230
feet, and also has an internal drug pump,
typically used for painkillers, because as

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:18.249
we are about to learn, SCP-2085-B is most
often on the wrong end of pain.

00:10:18.249 --> 00:10:22.670
Notice, these modifications are not those
you would find in a science-fiction novel

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:27.680
but more likely behind the trench coat of
a suspicious man in a dark alley.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.949
And we all know nothing good is ever concealed
behind a trench coat… but have you ever

00:10:31.949 --> 00:10:36.029
wondered if that truth also extends to robes?

00:10:36.029 --> 00:10:43.370
Because when we pull open SCP-2085’s what
we find is truly terrifying…

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.540
SCP-2085-1!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:53.790
SCP-2085-1 is a fibrous mass of self-replicating
carbon nanomaterials within SCP-2085-B’s

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:59.480
chest cavity, with growths protruding into
the liver, pancreas, gallbladder, spinal cord,

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.709
and left lung.

00:11:00.709 --> 00:11:08.990
The growth of the SCP-2085-1 and its consumption
of SCP-2085-B’s body tissues has been impeded

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:14.259
through the addition of various containment
implants used to sever communication between

00:11:14.259 --> 00:11:19.870
growth sections and control nodes and counter
the replication process.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:25.220
SCP-2085-1’s rate of replication without
the influence of these containment implants

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.990
is unknown.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:32.430
SCP-2085-1’s periods of activity occur,
on average, once every three months.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:39.809
The process lasts for up to fifteen minutes
and causes SCP-2085-B intense pain.

00:11:39.809 --> 00:11:41.660
Imagine a heart attack.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:45.200
Imagine Mike Tyson using your sternum like
a punching bag.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.589
Imagine a cactus strapped to your front.

00:11:47.589 --> 00:11:52.490
This is the pain and torture SCP-2085 wears
daily.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.079
There’s no S logo printed on his chest like
SuperMan.

00:11:56.079 --> 00:11:58.839
No symmetrically slick symbol like BatMan.

00:11:58.839 --> 00:12:01.749
Instead, just cancerous growth.

00:12:01.749 --> 00:12:03.809
Kryptonite worn like a tie.

00:12:03.809 --> 00:12:06.350
The knot never to be loosened.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:13.399
But to SCP-2085-B, this anomaly is not just
a number to be studied, but more so a being

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:14.899
to be understood.

00:12:14.899 --> 00:12:17.559
It is more personal than a medical condition.

00:12:17.559 --> 00:12:21.399
It is something he wakes up with each and
every day.

00:12:21.399 --> 00:12:22.560
He calls it Red.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:28.709
At first, The Foundation saw SCP-2085’s
close connection with Red to be childish and

00:12:28.709 --> 00:12:33.660
silly, as if a small boy who names his freckles
out of boredom and loneliness.

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:39.149
But as you are about to see, how they met
was more memorable than first finding a freckle

00:12:39.149 --> 00:12:40.220
in the mirror.

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:46.139
A meteor struck down, and SCP-2085-B was the
only person at the scene.

00:12:46.139 --> 00:12:47.580
Red was inside.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:52.199
As Wizard approached the meteor, Red leapt
onto him and buried a home into his chest

00:12:52.199 --> 00:12:53.350
cavity.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:57.450
Far from a freckle on the skin, Red is a cancer.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:13:00.670
It grows and grows, leeching to what it can.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.839
It can’t be removed with surgery.

00:13:02.839 --> 00:13:05.040
It can’t be covered by a Band-Aid.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.300
It has no empathy or mercy.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.920
It leeches on and eats away at its host.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.999
But it’s more than pain that it causes.

00:13:13.999 --> 00:13:18.670
Falling off a swing set and busting open your
leg hurts, sure, but at least both you and

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:21.249
your injury are on the same team.

00:13:21.249 --> 00:13:22.760
Cuts try to heal.

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.879
When left alone, injuries make effort to find
homeostasis.

00:13:26.879 --> 00:13:29.350
But Red is a different breed.

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:33.920
It hates us in a way that injuries are incapable
of doing.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:36.540
It has a deep disdain for humanity.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:40.680
It tears Wizard down, reveling in his degradation.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:44.199
Its sole purpose is to eat him whole.

00:13:44.199 --> 00:13:48.750
Wizard can only take this personally, as he
doesn’t just feel the universally understood

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:53.600
sensation of pain, but also the unique passion
of its purpose.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:59.579
SCP-2085-B’s adventure’s with Red seem
to be where our story begins, and what ultimately

00:13:59.579 --> 00:14:01.139
keeps it moving.

00:14:01.139 --> 00:14:07.360
In fact, it was while SCP-20850-B was running
around trying to fix his chest with implants

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:14.649
when he eventually met who we refer to as
SCP-2085-A-1 through A-5.

00:14:14.649 --> 00:14:18.860
He was at the clinic to get some new parts,
and when he was going through the installation

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.429
process there was an explosion.

00:14:21.429 --> 00:14:24.730
One of the five girls barged out of a building,
guns blazing.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.550
He started running alongside them with his
chest half open.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:31.600
The women embraced him immediately, and he
reciprocated.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.839
Knowing nothing of the situation, he instinctively
knew to take their side.

00:14:35.839 --> 00:14:40.249
There were bullets coming from both directions,
but he intuitively understood which side was

00:14:40.249 --> 00:14:47.990
good and which side was bad – a distinction
SCP-2085 believes the world needs help clarifying.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:53.170
But it is hard to see a reason for a war when
our eyes are focused on the casualties.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:56.079
Beliefs are less clear when tucked behind
bullets.

00:14:56.079 --> 00:14:58.680
The sounds of gunfire muffle their message.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:06.209
Morality, while a complex subject, SCP-2085
believes is simplified by the masses.

00:15:06.209 --> 00:15:11.069
Events are deemed good or bad based on the
term used for them in a court of law.

00:15:11.069 --> 00:15:16.569
When we see the words: smuggling, theft, assault,
vandalism, corporate sabotage, embezzlement,

00:15:16.569 --> 00:15:23.769
identity theft, fraud, copyright infringement,
piracy, and tax evasion, it is our impulse

00:15:23.769 --> 00:15:26.279
to label those as morally bad.

00:15:26.279 --> 00:15:31.139
But SCP-2085 desperately wants you to look
beyond the language.

00:15:31.139 --> 00:15:37.270
They want the words to dissipate off the paper,
letter by letter, until all you have is a

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.360
blank page.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:41.959
Now, look at the pencil and the hand that
holds it.

00:15:41.959 --> 00:15:43.579
Watch how it moves.

00:15:43.579 --> 00:15:45.509
That is what matters.

00:15:45.509 --> 00:15:48.679
Whether it draws weapons or mermaids is irrelevant.

00:15:48.679 --> 00:15:50.519
Both can be used for good.

00:15:50.519 --> 00:15:52.769
Both can be used for evil.

00:15:52.769 --> 00:15:54.699
Intent is everything.

00:15:54.699 --> 00:16:01.220
And SCP-2085 intends on making the world a
better place, or so they like to claim.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.940
But maybe there is more to it.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:09.339
After SCP-2085-B and the five women escaped
the gunfire, they went on to steal a boat

00:16:09.339 --> 00:16:11.230
and high tail it out of Japan.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:16.279
They spent their nights out there on the ocean,
stargazing and stuffing themselves with instant

00:16:16.279 --> 00:16:18.019
ramen and cheap beer.

00:16:18.019 --> 00:16:24.809
And, surprisingly, between all the crazy adventures
SCP-2085-B had been on, this is what Wizard

00:16:24.809 --> 00:16:26.309
spoke about most.

00:16:26.309 --> 00:16:29.029
The time spent on the boat out at sea.

00:16:29.029 --> 00:16:33.839
For the first time in ages, he was finally
somewhere where he was happy.

00:16:33.839 --> 00:16:37.730
It was this moment that actually meant the
most to him.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.740
It wasn’t the children they apparently saved
from imperialism.

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:44.699
It wasn’t the wealth they apparently redistributed
to the poor.

00:16:44.699 --> 00:16:46.369
It wasn’t any good deed at all.

00:16:46.369 --> 00:16:52.110
It was the selfish, almost shallow, sensation
of being happy on a boat.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:58.929
This singular moment meant so much to SCP-2085-B.
He reflected on it as if it were a wedding

00:16:58.929 --> 00:17:01.449
day or a memorable vacation.

00:17:01.449 --> 00:17:03.160
Which makes you wonder.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:08.659
SCP-2085 has been investigated and interrogated,
and all that they preach is that they are

00:17:08.659 --> 00:17:11.350
doing the world a favor with their antics.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.089
Their tales are captivating, sure.

00:17:13.089 --> 00:17:17.720
But is it actually story telling or is it
just virtue signaling?

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:23.930
There is an emotional depth to SCP-2085 unique
to any other militant anarchist group.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:28.300
While they are genetically designed to most
efficiently complete missions, they are not

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:32.200
at all robots fixed on the high of task completion.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.950
Each and every one of them wants more.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.080
They want a group.

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:40.330
They want a group not just to have the numbers
to overthrow a government, but to have the

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:45.120
numbers to fill a room, or boat, with companionship.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:49.410
When they refuse to cooperate with you and
leak information about their operation, maybe

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:54.530
what you are witnessing isn’t the strength
of their loyalty, but also the weakness of

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.880
their codependence.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:18:01.429
And so, you decide this is the new angle you’re
going to take with your interrogation.

00:18:01.429 --> 00:18:03.630
You enter the room with a new focus.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:07.549
You feel like an earthquake, eager to make
cracks in their core.

00:18:07.549 --> 00:18:09.559
You isolate SCP 2085-A-4.

00:18:09.559 --> 00:18:13.940
You are met, expectantly, with hostility.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.220
You fight back with psychology.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:20.880
You cross your legs and put on your glasses
as if to say, “Let’s talk about that anger.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.400
Where does it stem from?”

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.169
She strengthens her emotional guard.

00:18:24.169 --> 00:18:25.960
But you keep prying.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.190
You say that it sounds like she is lonely.

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:32.650
You say it sounds like her loyalty doesn’t
come from good character but rather insecurity

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.070
and self-doubt.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:38.409
You ask her if completing missions with her
crew was actually a way to improve the world

00:18:38.409 --> 00:18:43.400
or was it just an elaborate way to build a
close friend group bound together by common

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.400
goals.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.640
Did new missions sprout from necessity or
were they fabricated by fears of being alone

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.230
with nothing to do?

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:55.700
Were end of operation high-fives to celebrate
good overcoming evil or were they just excuses

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:59.730
to feel the touch of another human, skin to
skin.

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:04.120
You stop there and let silence do the rest.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.280
SCP 2085-A-4 sits with her thoughts.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.809
She is ready to break…and finally she does.

00:19:09.809 --> 00:19:13.610
She says she’s willing to provide video
logs of the group’s former operations.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.190
She’s ready to cooperate.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:20.149
She’s ready to abandon loyalty to groupthink
and focus instead on self-improvement.

00:19:20.149 --> 00:19:27.309
In exchange, she kindly asks that she be reciprocated
and that the sanction placed on her be lifted.

00:19:27.309 --> 00:19:31.500
You come to an agreement, and with that you
feel like your work is done.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:32.500
But is it?

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.590
You’re feeling cocky and accomplished.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:39.019
You forward the video logs to an isolated
network for D-class personnel to review and

00:19:39.019 --> 00:19:42.110
you sit back and enjoy a celebratory drink.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:46.770
You have infiltrated and broken the mind of
a genetically modified radical designed for

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:47.770
anarchy.

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:52.890
You give yourself a pat on the back, and you’re
feeling so great that the pat might even turn

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:58.559
into a massage, but before you can indulge
in that deep tissue level of self-admiration,

00:19:58.559 --> 00:19:59.830
the phone rings.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:03.070
Can it be a call from the president telling
you that you’re the greatest investigator

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.320
of all time?

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:08.409
Can it be that they need you to pose in front
of a world-renowned artist so that they can

00:20:08.409 --> 00:20:12.029
erect a statue of you in the center of town
square?

00:20:12.029 --> 00:20:15.860
But the panic on the other side of the phone
halts your daydream.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:21.240
Your stomach drops, as if a sudden plummet
from a perfectly vertical roller-coaster.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.100
You have fallen into a trap.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:28.769
The video log at the center of your negotiation
was not at all what it was promised to be.

00:20:28.769 --> 00:20:35.320
The file, titled backup.avi, consisted of
a two-hour long video of a feces-filled toilet,

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:40.700
presumably recorded from SCP-2085-A-4’s
point of view, accompanied by an audio loop

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:45.910
of the folk song “Korobeiniki”, as performed
by the Red Army Choir.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.840
Its absurdity feels like an art project.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:52.240
Like a short film you are assigned to watch
in a community college class.

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:55.750
But instead of putting you to sleep…it does
a whole lot more.

00:20:55.750 --> 00:21:01.350
The contained audio-visual cognitohazard induced
anaphylaxis and exudative diarrhea in the

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:03.130
observing D-Class subject.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:07.630
The D-Class subject died four minutes after
initial access of the file from blood loss

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.460
and oxygen deprivation.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:18.190
SCP-2085-A-4 sits in containment laughing,
while you sit there on your couch, dethroned,

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:23.649
back where you started, having thought you
tore SCP-2085 apart with your mind, only to

00:21:23.649 --> 00:21:27.770
learn that your efforts only reinforced it
with more glue.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:35.210
Now go check out “SCP-247 - A Harmless Kitten”
and “SCP-577 - Bullet Cat” for more SCPs

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.890
that’ll melt - or claw out - a cat lover’s
heart!

